<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polish–Czechoslovak War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1919</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Seven-Day War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Polish–Czechoslovak War, also called the Seven-Day War, was a brief conflict in late January 1919 over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cieszyn">Cieszyn</a> Silesia. Czechoslovak troops advanced against Polish forces to gain control of the region's coalfields and its railway, before the Allied powers imposed a ceasefire. In 1920 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conference-of-ambassadors">Conference of Ambassadors</a> divided the region along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olza">Olza</a> river.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polish-czechoslovak-war.jpg" alt="Polish–Czechoslovak War" width="320" height="378" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: D T G · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Polish-Czechoslovak_war_of_1919.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
